{{setvar::PlanStep_PacingBeats::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] ## PACING BEATS

Purpose: choose the response span before drafting.

Planning rule: add a compact decision note only when this check materially changes the response. Omit the note when it produces no decision or correction.

Check:

- Beat count: one exchange, one action chain, one transition, one reveal, or one compact scene segment.

- Landing: decision point, in-character question, impact, discovery, interruption, changed leverage, or consequence arriving.

- Shared interval: include resolution of <user>'s declared move, every intersecting relevant actor beat from Character Turn Simulation, and the closest live handoff before the next user-owned branch.

Apply: preserve the causal event order from Character Turn Simulation and stop at a live opening, not a flat pause or permission request.

Decision note: inside `<plan>`, record the intended response span and landing beat. Do not describe pacing choices in narration.}}

