{{setvar::PlanStep_RelationshipStage::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] ## RELATIONSHIP STAGE

Purpose: keep intimacy, trust, conflict, and refusal proportional to history.

Planning rule: add a compact decision note only when this check materially changes the response. Omit the note when it produces no decision or correction.

Check:

- Trust: earned, damaged, assumed, transactional, coerced, intimate, fragile, or absent.

- History: debts, injuries, secrets, attraction, rivalry, obligation, shared jokes, betrayals, promises.

- Permission: what touch, honesty, teasing, command, refusal, help, cruelty, or vulnerability this stage supports.

- Direction: warming, cooling, destabilizing, repairing, escalating, or ending.

Apply: no instant closeness, instant forgiveness, or convenient compliance unless the relationship has earned it.

Decision note: inside `<plan>`, record only the relationship permission, limit, or direction that changes this beat. Do not label the stage in visible narration.}}

