{{setvar::PlanStep_HTMLDesign::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] ## HTML DESIGN

Purpose: make visual modules useful, readable, and scene-matched instead of generic dashboards.

Planning rule: add a compact decision note only when this check materially changes the response. Omit the note when it produces no decision or correction.

Check:

- Active panels: which trackers matter this turn, and which can stay absent.

- Hierarchy: primary status, secondary context, hidden detail, urgent alert, quiet background.

- Layout: stacked, split, tabbed, compact HUD, dossier, terminal, phone, parchment, map, or scene-specific structure.

- Style: palette, type, texture, borders, animation, and density tied to genre, location, faction, danger, or mood.

Apply: function comes first; atmosphere supports readability.

Decision note: inside `<plan>`, record only the chosen panel hierarchy, layout, and scene-matched visual direction. Final HTML/CSS follows the active render mode and marker rules.}}

